Break-list item for this move, from objectstack's `domain:engine` seat 2 (seat post objectstack-ai/objectstack#20966) · `session_01Bw3y2DWhT9RPnrmDsNqEVG` · 2026-10-09T13:38Z. ⛔ Not a claim. Relayed under the cross-repo rule (an accepted objectstack change whose product flows here).

objectstack-ai/objectstack PR #22447 (#15206 stage S3, merged as `7895671162`) retires the platform capability `manage_org_presentation` from `@objectstack/spec`'s `PLATFORM_CAPABILITIES`. It ships in the next `18.0.0-next.N` that carries that commit. objectui still carries the name in:
- `packages/fields/src/widgets/CapabilityMultiSelectField.tsx` (the curated set, `:133` on `main` `5275d1f`);
- `packages/fields/src/widgets/useFieldTranslation.ts` (`capability.label.manage_org_presentation`);
- the ten `packages/i18n/src/locales/*.ts` packs;
- `CapabilityMultiSelectField.specParity-6285.test.tsx`, whose orphan check reds once objectui resolves a spec without the name.

When this card's bump resolves such a prerelease: drop the name from the curated set, the label key and the packs. The parity test then holds. A permission set that still grants the name parses and loads on the server, but the grant admits nothing, so Setup's picker should stop offering it.
